Package: sayri
Version: 0.1.3
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Jaime <info@inled.es>
Depends: python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-webkit-6.0, libgtk4-layer-shell0, python3-httpx, pipewire
Suggests: whisper.cpp, grim, ydotool
Description: Siri-like voice assistant for Pulsar OS (GTK4).
 Sayri is an always-available Siri-style assistant. A reactive orb pinned to
 the top-left corner of the screen reacts to your voice: whisper.cpp
 transcribes what you say, the text appears in an Apple-intelligence style
 cajita (with a chroma-ring animated border) right next to the orb, and when
 you pause (or press Enter) the query is sent to any OpenAI-compatible API
 (OpenAI, Ollama, LM Studio, OpenClaw, ...). The answer is spoken back with
 Piper TTS while the orb animates.
 .
 Clicking the orb toggles the microphone on/off; the cajita is also the text
 input and shows settings/quit. A GTK4 settings window downloads whisper.cpp
 models and Piper voices per language and configures the provider (endpoint,
 key, model, ...).
 .
 whisper.cpp and Piper binaries are detected on PATH; if missing, the
 settings window can download static builds and models on first use.
